ia platform lock-in, brand enclosure, or capital-weighted governance.\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"enterprise_stack_levels\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"from_push_to_pull\",\n      \"name\": \"From Push to Pull\",\n      \"traditional\": \"Decentralise and thus add flexibility to company processes in order to be more customer-focused. To respond rapidly and flexibly to new customers' needs, any part of the value chain including production or even research and development may be affected.\",\n      \"p2p_description\": \"Open your operations to incluse early adapters or potential users / beneficiaries in your processes, integrating their needs into development of your offer.\",\n      \"material_distributed\": \"\",\n      \"examples\": \"\",\n      \"dependability_measures\": \"\",\n      \"ovn_fit\": \"medium\",\n      \"adaptation_rule\": \"Keep contribution accounting and commons access; avoid enclosure of the shared layer; prefer transparency over opaque capture.\",\n      \"risks\": \"Capture via platform lock-in, brand enclosure, or capital-weighted governance.\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"enterprise_stack_levels\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"guaranteed_availability\",\n      \"name\": \"Guaranteed Availability\",\n      \"traditional\": \"This pattern makes the customer's needs central to desicions within the enterprise and the shaping of the value proposition, it can be applied to all aspects of the business.\",\n      \"p2p_description\": \"Make your beneficiaries' need central to the organization, shaping your decisions and your value proposition.\",\n      \"material_distributed\": \"\",\n      \"examples\": \"\",\n      \"dependability_measures\": \"\",\n      \"ovn_fit\": \"medium\",\n      \"adaptation_rule\": \"Keep contribution accounting and commons access; avoid enclosure of the shared layer; prefer transparency over opaque capture.\",\n      \"risks\": \"Capture via platform lock-in, brand enclosure, or capital-weighted governance.\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"enterprise_stack_levels\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"hidden_revenue\",\n      \"name\": \"Hidden Revenue\",\n      \"traditional\": \"The logic that the income of the business depends on the users is abandoned. instead, the main source of revenue comes from a third party, who cross-finances whatever free or low-priced offering attracts the user. A very common application is financing through advertising.\",\n      \"p2p_description\": \"Your sustainability is linked not directly with your beneficiaries but with third parties. These third parties source your operations to attract users. Ex. financing through advertizing.\",\n      \"material_distributed\": \"\",\n      \"examples\": \"\",\n      \"dependability_measures\": \"\",\n      \"ovn_fit\": \"medium\",\n      \"adaptation_rule\": \"Keep contribution accounting and commons access; avoid enclosure of the shared layer; prefer transparency over opaque capture.\",\n      \"risks\": \"Capture via platform lock-in, brand enclosure, or capital-weighted governance.\",\n      \"flags\": [\n        \"use_with_caution\"\n      ],\n      \"enterprise_stack_levels\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ingredient_branding\",\n      \"name\": \"Ingredient Branding\",\n      \"traditional\": \"This is the inclusion of a branded ingredient originating from different suppliers into a product. The principal product is then advertised as containing the ingredient product and stressing the added value it brings to the customer.\",\n      \"p2p_description\": \"Include an very well-known and prized ingredient in your offering. Your offering will be noticed for containing that special ingredient. This ingredient can also be immaterial (ex. fair trade label) and even intangible (ex. spiritual dimension).\",\n      \"material_distributed\": \"\",\n      \"examples\": \"\",\n      \"dependability_measures\": \"\",\n      \"ovn_fit\": \"medium\",\n      \"adaptation_rule\": \"Keep contribution accounting and commons access; avoid enclosure of the shared layer; prefer transparency over opaque capture.\",\n      \"risks\": \"Capture via platform lock-in, brand enclosure, or capital-weighted governance.\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"enterprise_stack_levels\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"integrator\",\n      \"name\": \"Integrator\",\n      \"traditional\": \"A company functioning on the integrator model has command of the majority of the steps in the value-adding process including all resources and capabilities in terms of value creation. Efficiency gains economies of scope and reduces dependency on suppliers.\",\n      \"p2p_description\": \"Reduce dependency on other entities in your ecosystem, produce your offerings from A to Z, independently. Reduce costs and gain better control over the process, applying your own methods and tools. You may have efficiency gains, economy of scope, control your risk.\",\n      \"material_distributed\": \"\",\n      \"examples\": \"\",\n      \"dependability_measures\": \"\",\n      \"ovn_fit\": \"medium\",\n      \"adaptation_rule\": \"Keep contribution accounting and commons access; avoid enclosure of the shared layer; prefer transparency over opaque capture.\",\n      \"risks\": \"Capture via platform lock-in, brand enclosure, or capital-weighted governance.\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"enterprise_stack_levels\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"layer_player\",\n      \"name\": \"Layer Player\",\n      \"traditional\": \"A layer player is a specialized company limited to providing one value-adding step to different value chains. This step is typically offered within a variety of independent markets and industries. The company benefits from the economies of scale and often leads to more efficient production\",\n      \"p2p_description\": \"Your offering constitutes a layer in a larger offering from other actors, one value-added step to different value  chains. Efficnent production because specialization, benefit from scale. Ex. local food basket, composed of offerings from various small local producers.\",\n      \"material_distributed\": \"\",\n      \"examples\": \"\",\n      \"dependability_measures\": \"\",\n      \"ovn_fit\": \"medium\",\n      \"adaptation_rule\": \"Keep contribution accounting and commons access; avoid enclosure of the shared layer; prefer transparency over opaque capture.\",\n      \"risks\": \"Capture via platform lock-in, brand enclosure, or capital-weighted governance.\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"enterprise_stack_levels\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"leverage_customer_user_data\",\n      \"name\": \"Leverage Customer / user Data\",\n      \"traditional\": \"New value is created using customer data and preparing it in beneficial ways for internal usage or transmission of interested third parties. Revenues are generated by either selling this data directly to others or leveraging them for the company's own purpouses\",\n      \"p2p_description\": \"Leverage the data produced by participants, build analysis or dashboard services or provide it to third parties (which is not necesarelly bad in a p2p system where transparency is inportant and information must flow).\",\n      \"material_distributed\": \"\",\n      \"examples\": \"\",\n      \"dependability_measures\": \"\",\n      \"ovn_fit\": \"medium\",\n      \"adaptation_rule\": \"Keep contribution accounting and commons access; avoid enclosure of the shared layer; prefer transparency over opaque capture.\",\n      \"risks\": \"Capture via platform lock-in, brand enclosure, or capital-weighted governance.\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"enterprise_stack_levels\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"licensing\",\n      \"name\": \"Licensing\",\n      \"traditional\": \"The efforts are focused on developing intellectual property that can be licensed to other manufacturers. This model attempts to transform these intangible assets into money. Licensing gives the company the freedom to focus on R&D.\",\n      \"p2p_description\": \"control who can distribute your offering. Can simply be achieved by contracting with other parties, even if the technology on which your offerings are built is open source. Allows an agent to focus ion innovation and let other agents take on production and distribution.\",\n      \"material_distributed\": \"\",\n      \"examples\": \"\",\n      \"dependability_measures\": \"\",\n      \"ovn_fit\": \"medium\",\n      \"adaptation_rule\": \"Keep contribution accounting and commons access; avoid enclosure of the shared layer; prefer transparency over opaque capture.\",\n      \"risks\": \"Capture via platform lock-in, brand enclosure, or capital-weighted governance.\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"enterprise_stack_levels\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"lock_in\",\n      \"name\": \"Lock-in\",\n      \"traditional\": \"Customers are locked into a vendor's world of products and services. Transferring customs to another vendor is impossible without incurring substantial switching costs. This mechanism is affected either by technological mechanism or a high level of the interdependency of products and services.\",\n      \"p2p_description\": \"Provide an ecosystem of highly interoperable or interdependent offerings, which generates switching costs or network effects.\",\n      \"material_distributed\": \"\",\n      \"examples\": \"\",\n      \"dependability_measures\": \"\",\n      \"ovn_fit\": \"medium\",\n      \"adaptation_rule\": \"Keep contribution accounting and commons access; avoid enclosure of the shared layer; prefer transparency over opaque capture.\",\n      \"risks\": \"Capture via platform lock-in, brand enclosure, or capital-weighted governance.\",\n      \"flags\": [\n        \"use_with_caution\"\n      ],\n      \"enterprise_stack_levels\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"long_tail\",\n      \"name\": \"Long Tail\",\n      \"traditional\": \"The main bulk of revenues is generated through a long tail of nice products, which individually neither demand high volumes nor allow a high margin. If a wide variety of these products is offered in sufficient amounts, the profits from the accumulated small sales can add up.\",\n      \"p2p_description\": \"Your sustainability rests on a large number of niche offerings (low demand), not on a small number of offerings.\",\n      \"material_distributed\": \"\",\n      \"examples\": \"\",\n      \"dependability_measures\": \"\",\n      \"ovn_fit\": \"medium\",\n      \"adaptation_rule\": \"Keep contribution accounting and commons access; avoid enclosure of the shared layer; prefer transparency over opaque capture.\",\n      \"risks\": \"Capture via platform lock-in, brand enclosure, or capital-weighted governance.\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"enterprise_stack_levels\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"make_more_of_it\",\n      \"name\": \"Make More of it\",\n      \"traditional\": \"Know-how and other assets available in the company's are not only used to build its own products but are also offered to other companies. Thus sluck resources are used to create additional value besides those generated directly by the company's core value proposition.\",\n      \"p2p_description\": \"Offer excess capacity (resources and even time/know-how) in your organizations to other organizations in exchange for benefits. Don't just focus on your own offerings.\",\n      \"material_distributed\": \"\",\n      \"examples\": \"\",\n      \"dependability_measures\": \"\",\n      \"ovn_fit\": \"medium\",\n      \"adaptation_rule\": \"Keep contribution accounting and commons access; avoid enclosure of the shared layer; prefer transparency over opaque capture.\",\n      \"risks\": \"Capture via platform lock-in, brand enclosure, or capital-weighted governance.\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"enterprise_stack_levels\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"mass_customization\",\n      \"name\": \"Mass Customization\",\n      \"traditional\": \"Customising products through mass production once seemed to be an impossible endeavor, but this has now changed with the development of modular products and production systems that enable efficient individualization of product.\",\n      \"p2p_description\": \"Modular and highly customizable offerings and systems por production (digital fabrication), individualize the offering.\",\n      \"material_distributed\": \"\",\n      \"examples\": \"\",\n      \"dependability_measures\": \"\",\n      \"ovn_fit\": \"medium\",\n      \"adaptation_rule\": \"Keep contribution accounting and commons access; avoid enclosure of the shared layer; prefer transparency over opaque capture.\",\n      \"risks\": \"Capture via platform lock-in, brand enclosure, or capital-weighted governance.\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"enterprise_stack_levels\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"no_frills\",\n      \"name\": \"No Frills\",\n      \"traditional\": \"No frills value creation focuses on the necessary minimum to deliver the core value proposition of a product or service, which will thus typically be very basic. Cost savings are shared with the customer, usually resulting in a customer base with lower purchasing power or purchasing willingness.\",\n      \"p2p_description\": \"Your offering is basic, simple, very cost effective. Your offer can reach the poor.\",\n      \"material_distributed\": \"\",\n      \"examples\": \"\",\n      \"dependability_measures\": \"\",\n      \"ovn_fit\": \"medium\",\n      \"adaptation_rule\": \"Keep contribution accounting and commons access; avoid enclosure of the shared layer; prefer transparency over opaque capture.\",\n      \"risks\": \"Capture via platform lock-in, brand enclosure, or capital-weighted governance.\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"enterprise_stack_levels\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"open_bussiness\",\n      \"name\": \"Open Bussiness\",\n      \"traditional\": \"Collaboration with partners in the ecosystem becomes a central source of value creation. companies pursuing an open business model actively search novel ways of working together with suppliers, customers or complementors, to open up and extend their business.\",\n      \"p2p_description\": \"Integrate your organization with other actors in your ecosystem, become master of leveraging relations within the ecosystem, build synergies and collaborations. Your offering and the experience associated with it are prpoduced through this collaboration.\",\n      \"material_distributed\": \"Open-Value-networks (OVN) act as ecosystem builders in the CBPP transactional setting. Classical economies assign costs and resources to manufacture products. In CBPP, classical operations fall and tasks are to be handled by a large network of collaborators. Building this ecosystem requires innovative tools and methods to adapt to this new transactional setting.\",\n      \"examples\": \"\",\n      \"dependability_measures\": \"\",\n      \"ovn_fit\": \"medium\",\n      \"adaptation_rule\": \"Keep contribution accounting and commons access; avoid enclosure of the shared layer; prefer transparency over opaque capture.\",\n      \"risks\": \"Capture via platform lock-in, brand enclosure, or capital-weighted governance.\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"enterprise_stack_levels\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"open_source\",\n      \"name\": \"Open Source\",\n      \"traditional\": \"In open source software engineering, the source code of a product is not proprietary but is made freely accessible for anyone. Money is typically earned with services that are complimentary to the product, such as consulting and support.\",\n      \"p2p_description\": \"Your sustainability comes from offering services complementary to open source offering(s), which are not a products, themselves are not sold. Ex. consulting support\",\n      \"material_distributed\": \"\",\n      \"examples\": \"\",\n      \"dependability_measures\": \"\",\n      \"ovn_fit\": \"medium\",\n      \"adaptation_rule\": \"Keep contribution accounting and commons access; avoid enclosure of the shared layer; prefer transparency over opaque capture.\",\n      \"risks\": \"Capture via platform lock-in, brand enclosure, or capital-weighted governance.\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"enterprise_stack_levels\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"orchestrator\",\n      \"name\": \"Orchestrator\",\n      \"traditional\": \"The company's focus is on the core competencies within the value chain. The other segments of the value chain are outsourced and actively coordinated. This allows the company to reduce costs and to benefit from suppliers' economies of scale.\",\n      \"p2p_description\": \"Take a central role within your economic ecosystem by focusing on a key offering that holds this ecosystem tegether. You make it your responsability to coordinate complementary offerings provided by other actors. Thus, reduce costs (delegating production of peripherial offerings) and benefit from economy of scale.\",\n      \"material_distributed\": \"\",\n      \"examples\": \"\",\n      \"dependability_measures\": \"\",\n      \"ovn_fit\": \"medium\",\n      \"adaptation_rule\": \"Keep contribution accounting and commons access; avoid enclosure of the shared layer; prefer transparency over opaque capture.\",\n      \"risks\": \"Capture via platform lock-in, brand enclosure, or capital-weighted governance.\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"enterprise_stack_levels\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"pay_per_use\",\n      \"name\": \"Pay Per Use\",\n      \"traditional\": \"In this model, the actual usage of a service or product is metered. The customer pays on the basis of what he or she effectivelly consumes. The company is able to attract customers who whish to benefit from the additional flexibility, which might be priced higher.\",\n      \"p2p_description\": \"The usage of your offering is metered and your benefit is in proportion to the use that your beneficiaries make of it. You offer flexibility to your beneficiaries.\",\n      \"material_distributed\": \"\",\n      \"examples\": \"\",\n      \"dependability_measures\": \"\",\n      \"ovn_fit\": \"medium\",\n      \"adaptation_rule\": \"Keep contribution accounting and commons access; avoid enclosure of the shared layer; prefer transparency over opaque capture.\",\n      \"risks\": \"Capture via platform lock-in, brand enclosure, or capital-weighted governance.\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"enterprise_stack_levels\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"pay_what_you_want\",\n      \"name\": \"Pay What You Want\",\n      \"traditional\": \"The buyer pays any desired amount for a given commodity, sometimes even zero. In some cases, a minimum floor price may be set, and/or a suggested price may be indicated as guidance for the buyer. The customer is allowed to influence the price, while the seller benefits from the higher numbers of attracted customers, since individuals' willingness to pay is met. Based on the existance of social norms and morals, this is onnly rarely exploited, which makes it suitable to attract new customers.\",\n      \"p2p_description\": \"Your offering is entirelly free to access / use / consume. You may suggest a sinbolic or minimum reciprocation. Benefit from high number of users / beneficiaries and allow some of them to reward you very much.\",\n      \"material_distributed\": \"\",\n      \"examples\": \"\",\n      \"dependability_measures\": \"\",\n      \"ovn_fit\": \"medium\",\n      \"adaptation_rule\": \"Keep contribution accounting and commons access; avoid enclosure of the shared layer; prefer transparency over opaque capture.\",\n      \"risks\": \"Capture via platform lock-in, brand enclosure, or capital-weighted governance.\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"enterprise_stack_levels\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"peer_to_peer\",\n      \"name\": \"Peer-to-Peer\",\n      \"traditional\": \"This model is based on a